{
 "as_of": "2026-10-05",
 "descriptor": "Optical fibre cable, telecom equipment and defence",
 "lede": "A telecom-equipment and EPC company that has become an optical-fibre exporter to US hyperscalers, with a defence arm on the side. Margins and orders have jumped and the MD raised FY27 growth to 40%+, but cash flow has not followed, receivables top ₹2,000 Cr and the promoter stake keeps falling.",
 "market": {
  "price": 250,
  "mcap_cr": 38372,
  "pe": 67.0,
  "pb": 7.8,
  "ev_ebitda": 35
 },
 "short_version": [
  {
   "lead": "What's going right",
   "text": "Q1 FY27 revenue +120% to ₹1,915 Cr with a 23.3% reported EBITDA margin and PAT of ₹246 Cr; order book ₹26,665 Cr (5x FY26 revenue) including a ~$1.1 billion OFC contract; exports now over half of revenue."
  },
  {
   "lead": "What to be sceptical about",
   "text": "Operating cash flow was –₹378 Cr in FY26 and cumulative cash flow covers only ~28% of FY22-26 profit; debtor days ~163 and inventory days 191. Promoter holding fell to 28.3%, with warrants and a defence restructuring that leaves HFCL with part ownership."
  },
  {
   "lead": "Price",
   "text": "67x trailing earnings (about 35x EV/EBITDA); on Q1 annualised profit nearer 39x, cheaper than Sterlite."
  }
 ],
 "sections": [
  {
   "id": "business",
   "title": "Company overview and business model",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "HFCL makes optical fibre and fibre-optic cable (including high-fibre-count IBR cables for data centres), data-centre connectivity products (via subsidiary HTL), telecom equipment (radios, routers, Wi-Fi), and defence products (radars, thermal sights, fuzes, aerostructures after an acquisition). It also runs telecom EPC projects such as BharatNet and the Army's network.",
     "src": "Jul call p.2"
    },
    {
     "type": "tiles",
     "items": [
      {
       "value": "₹26,665 Cr",
       "label": "Order book, June 2026"
      },
      {
       "value": "~55%",
       "label": "Exports share of Q1 FY27 revenue"
      },
      {
       "value": "28 → 34 mn fkm",
       "label": "Fibre capacity by Dec 2026"
      },
      {
       "value": "₹800 Cr",
       "label": "Expected FY27 data-centre connectivity revenue"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "bullets",
     "title": "Where the profit comes from",
     "items": [
      {
       "lead": "",
       "text": "Telecom products (mainly OFC) earn ~30% segment margins; EPC has been loss-making on the Army network warranty.",
       "src": "Jul call p.10"
      },
      {
       "lead": "",
       "text": "Keeps some capacity unsold to capture higher spot prices.",
       "src": "May call p.12"
      },
      {
       "lead": "",
       "text": "A ₹580 Cr preform plant should cut preform cost ~30% vs buying.",
       "src": "Jul call p.18"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "bullets",
     "title": "What changed in 3–5 years",
     "items": [
      {
       "lead": "",
       "text": "Exports rose from 4.5% of revenue (FY21) to 41% (FY26); products from 27% to 62%.",
       "src": "May call p.6"
      },
      {
       "lead": "",
       "text": "Government share of the order book fell from 51% to 37%.",
       "src": "May call p.6"
      },
      {
       "lead": "",
       "text": "Defence consolidated into HFCL Advance Systems with an aerospace acquisition.",
       "src": "May call p.5"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
